  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Satendra Kumar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 13 April, 2024 Author: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia Bench: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia 1 M.Cr.C.No.40838/2023 IN THE HIGH COURT OF MADHYA PRADESH AT JABALPUR BEFORE HON'BLE SHRI JUSTICE GURPAL SINGH AHLUWALIA ON THE 13th OF APRIL, 2024 MISC. CRIMINAL CASE No. 40838 of 2023 BETWEEN:- 1. SATENDRA KUMAR S/O SHRI MEWA RAM, AGED ABOUT 53 YEARS, OCCUPATION: SELF EMPLOYED R/O 705-D-16/2 WARD NO 03 NEAR AAMBAGH MOHROLI NEW DELHI MANDIR MARG NEW DELHI 2. SEEMA DEVI W/O SATENDRA KUMAR, AGED ABOUT 55 YEARS, OCCUPATION: HOUSE WIFE R/O 705- D-16/2, WARD NO.03, NEAR AAMBAGH MOHROLI, NEW DELHI MANDIR MARG, NEW DELHI (DELHI) .....APPLICANTS (BY SHRI VIVEK AGRAWAL - ADVOCATE ) AND 1. THE STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH THROUGH P.S. MAHILA THANA BHOPAL CITY DISTRICT BHOPAL (MADHYA PRADESH) 2. SMT. NEETU OAD W/O SANJEEV KUMAR, AGED ABOUT 31 YEARS, R/O H.NO.63 ISHAAN PARK PATEL NAGAR RAISEN ROAD, POLICE STATION PIPLANI BHOPAL DISTRICT BHOPAL (MADHYA PRADESH) .....RESPONDENTS (SHRI DILIP PARIHAR - PANEL LAWYER FOR THE RESPODNENT Satendra Kumar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 13 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/199347337/ 1 NO.1/STATE ) ........................................................................................ This petition coming on for admission this day, the court passed the following: ORDER",
    "facts": "The respondent no.2 lodged an FIR against the applicants as well as their son Sanjeev Kumar on the allegations that she got married to Sanjeev Kumar on 10.12.2022. Thus, it is clear that applicant no.1 was deliberately and in a planned manner was preparing false defence.",
    "arguments": "Once the son of the applicants is also residing with the applicants then giving of an information to Police Station Mehrauli on 31.5.2021 prima facie appears to be a defence to overcome an eventuality, which may arise in future. If the applicant no.1 was so disturbed with the uncivilized behavior of his son then why he was not ousted from the house. Satendra Kumar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 13 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/199347337/ 3 10. It is further submitted that the Court owes a duty to look into many other attending circumstances emerging from the record of the case over and above averments and, if need be, with due care and circumspection, to try and read between the lines."
  },
