          },
          {
            "pattern": "\\bquashed\\b",
            "matched_text": "quashed",
            "start": 429,
            "end": 436
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "This application under section 482 of CrPC has been filed seeking the following relief(s) :-\n\"It is therefore prayed to the Hon'ble Court may be please to allow the petition and quashed the FIR dated 03.06.2023 as well as charge sheet dated"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4c9d1c17cb2d4eee9d69d2e86296bf56_42",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is suffice to mention here that even this complaint does not bear any acknowledgment of receipt."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c0d2e16960414a1288c126a000afb7b3_43",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However, this complaint clearly throws a light on the fact that the son of the applicants is residing with the applicants because in complaint dated 5.5.2023 the applicant no.1 has specifically admitted that the applicants as well as his so"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "24c7c90f92bb49da88593fb324839d30_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. Thus, it is clear that the son of the applicants is still residing with them."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9a99a6955a174ba794517b100e4a60f1_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The necessity of preparing false defence, by itself indicates that applicants had guilty mind."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9df684e9a9124c9fb161791c8dbf5f03_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n11. So far as the contention of the counsel for applicants that as per the written declaration dated 4.5.2023 the respondent no.2 had left her matrimonial house on 4.5.2023; whereas as per the FIR,\nthe incident took place on 5.5.2023, ther"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "93d99625d7804a53bc67be0f771a0630_51",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "What was the need of giving an information to the Police Station Mehrauli, New Delhi, is a question, which is to be explained by the applicants in the trial."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "955e8529fc864588808bdc30e3d09925_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The written declaration is not addressed to anybody."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0b08fd4fa2cc41b1917fcc386d178574_53",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, it is prima facie clear that the respondent no.2 must not have gone to the Police Station Mehrauli, New Delhi to give information about her departure from the matrimonial house."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "789f8e08b31d405fbd96fafad8116e63_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "12. Since it is a private document, therefore, it is required to be proved and this Court cannot take cognizance of the same in support of the defence of the applicants."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "29010978e0fc49aa8e5553760e552a06_55",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "13. So far as the discrepancy with regard to the date of incident as to whether the respondent no.2 was ousted from her matrimonial house on 4.5.2023 or 5.5.2023, it is suffice to mention here that undue importance cannot be given to such a"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bb080ef12f4a4cc0980a93693a433fb3_56",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There are specific allegations of harassment, passing of taunts and breaking of mobile phone by the applicants or applicant no.1.\n14."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "62af068a4f6640cabdc68989d44152a8_57",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Supreme Court in the case of Taramani Parakh Vs. State of Madhya Pradesh and Others reported in (2015) 11 SCC 260 has held as under:-\n\"12."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "878378de8fbd4e2cbf70476ac11591b5_58",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In Kailash Chandra Agrawal v. State of U.P. [Kailash Chandra Agrawal v. State of U.P., (2014) 16 SCC 551] , it was observed (SCC p. 553, paras 8-9):\n\"8."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bb4802cf11094396a7b649a1a04157da_59",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "We have gone through the FIR and the criminal complaint."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5d4e0248532a45cbbc3c204bee9160fb_60",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the FIR, the appellants have not been named and in the criminal complaint they have been named without attributing any specific role to them."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a0be0973fad24c5cbd6f954d1d1c1857_61",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The relationship of the appellants with the husband of the complainant is distant."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "98549e1064cf4ceaa1d4d5c3919e3bdf_62",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In Kans Raj v. State of Punjab [Kans Raj v.\nState of Punjab, (2000) 5 SCC 207 : 2000 SCC (Cri) 935 : (2000) 3 SCR 662] it was observed (SCC p. 217, para 5):\n\"5. ... A tendency has, however, developed for roping in all relations of the in-la"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e72b88f5b31c45a18dcce64c5fbe1e08_63",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In their overenthusiasm and anxiety to seek conviction for maximum people, the parents of the deceased have been found to be making efforts for involving other relations which ultimately weaken the case of the prosecution even against the r"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "39f1bca4d3104ed5b397b7da7dd1e3c4_64",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nSatendra Kumar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 13 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/199347337/\n4"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1b532366912a4ecc9223eb478b09cfb9_65",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Court has, thus, to be careful in summoning distant relatives without there being specific material."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "29721bf89533467d8ea8db80e8df823d_66",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Only the husband, his parents or at best close family members may be expected to demand dowry or to harass the wife but not distant relations, unless there is tangible material to support allegations made against such distant relations."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c64564ee2431423cb6faca9c138c2a3a_67",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Mere naming of distant relations is not enough to summon them in the absence of any specific role and material to support such role."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fabe7f51e13d42f38ad99d41b7a4a5fa_68",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. The parameters for quashing proceedings in a criminal complaint are well known."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3ba75d0673dd4858a22fe2ade97bc1ae_69",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "If there are triable issues, the Court is not expected to go into the veracity of the rival versions but where on the face of it, the criminal proceedings are abuse of Court's process, quashing jurisdiction can be exercised."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ea0093271fe14f468d9a84d11316f83f_70",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Reference may be made to K. Ramakrishna v. State of Bihar [K. Ramakrishna v. State of Bihar, (2000) 8 SCC 547 : 2001 SCC (Cri) 27] , Pepsi Foods Ltd. v. Judicial Magistrate [Pepsi Foods Ltd. v. Judicial Magistrate, (1998) 5 SCC 749 :\n1998 S"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d3c79c58afc5492f966da7b9d949a2a1_71",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the present case, the complaint is as follows:\n\"Sir, it is submitted that I was married on 18- 11-2009 with Sidharath Parakh s/o Manak Chand Parakh r/o Sarafa Bazar in front of Radha Krishna Market, Gwalior according to the Hindu rites a"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "49b913a7e5534f9a855aff980e6c1f71_72",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the marriage my father had given gold and silver ornaments, cash amount and household goods according to his capacity."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b3b0c4580be34c9e8722a2afa15e5637_73",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nAfter the marriage when I went to my matrimonial home, I was treated nicely by the members of the family."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f25ba4757854459ea08b1f631050aeaa_74",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "When on the second occasion I went to my matrimonial home, my husband, father-in-law and mother-in-law started harassing me for not bringing the dowry and started saying that I should bring from my father 25-30 tolas of gold and Rs 2,00,000"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "eadd3c93e919423ba55b9010e10508a1_75",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "On account of this my husband also used to beat me and my father-in-law and my mother-in-law used to torture me by giving the taunts."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "01ad259ba948473f9fe3d8101396be03_76",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In this connection I used to tell my father Kundanmal Oswal, my mother Smt Prem Lata Oswal, uncle Ashok Rai Sharma and uncle Ved Prakash Mishra from time to time."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "131cd3a5b4ba47c3934fe0da64cf015b_77",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "On 2-4-2010 the members of the family of my matrimonial home forcibly sent me to the house of my parents in Ganj Basoda along with my brother Deepak."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0a4f905b2c9d472eb6ea4c44aa29302b_78",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "They snatched my clothes and ornaments and kept with them."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d156a1b945314b66a30c6d91cdb3a0c7_79",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Since then till today my husband has been harassing me on the telephone and has not come to take me back."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fb53ac811d824d519263a25970e3c8b3_80",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Being compelled, I have been moving this application before you."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "671a858cf712470ba66d5f7e53ff0b15_81",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Sir, it is prayed that Satendra Kumar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 13 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/199347337/\n5 action be taken against husband Sidharath Parakh, my father-in-law Manak Chand Parakh and my mot"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c70ae50905894ceeb6636a315b409e07_82",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "From a reading of the complaint, it cannot be held that even if the allegations are taken as proved no case is made out."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e21d94f8490940d9b8c48828d4030246_83",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There are allegations against Respondent 2 and his parents for harassing the complainant which forced her to leave the matrimonial home."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4f4fbc78dd31476689e3941b4296d651_84",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Even now she continues to be separated from the matrimonial home as she apprehends lack of security and safety and proper environment in the matrimonial home."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5e41eefa19ea4fd691a21fac1b1299c3_85",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The question whether the appellant has in fact been harassed and treated with cruelty is a matter of trial but at this stage, it cannot be said that no case is made out."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "41e0fd3fb04e4cfbb6171cf3f74ad1df_86",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus, quashing of proceedings before the trial is not permissible.\""
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4d3bb7993eff40b3b9ad78d82d4fad87_87",
        "summary_section": "arguments",
        "labels": [
          "ARG_PETITIONER"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
            "pattern": "\\bquashed\\b",
            "matched_text": "quashed",
            "start": 234,
            "end": 241
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "15. The counsel for the petitioner has relied upon the judgment passed by the Supreme Court in the case of Abhishek Vs. State of M.P., decided on 31st August, 2023 in Criminal Appeal No.1457/2015 to submit that the proceedings can be quashe"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ff3b6f94e588499886197a1184d10a62_89",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "16. If the facts of the present case are concerned, this Court has already considered that what was the need for the respondent no.2 to give in writing before leaving her matrimonial house."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7360b6fd062f4bd2800d15fd79b9ba31_90",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "That shows that the relationship was strained."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0bf1b14d379a416dbf164a61f554c071_91",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Even otherwise in the written declaration, it was specifically mentioned by the respondent no.2 that on account of dispute with her in-laws she is going back to her parental home."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5ecd0b325ba24d5a89b61daf85a44fd3_92",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Furthermore, the applicants have also not explained that once the applicant no.1 has disowned his son Sanjeev Kumar then why Sanjeev Kumar was allowed to stay in the house of the applicants itself."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fa37fa5b19ec446ea8cf26a8d7def9db_93",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "17. Thus considering the circumstances, this Court is of the considered opinion that there is a prima facie case warranting prosecution of the applicants no.1 and 2.\n18."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "26ea1ee695b14733bf28bd1c54223484_94",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Accordingly, no case is made out warranting interference."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c6752caadc5e4d1c87a1432e2250bf42_95",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "19. The application fails and is hereby dismissed."
      }
